==Battleground==
*3 [[The Thrillerz|Thrillerz]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Sir Seal]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*3 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Pterowl Hazuku]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
**5 [[The Thrillerz|Thrillerz]] spawn, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
**3 [[Zomboe]]s spawn, delay 43.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,400f</sup>.
**5 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The most difficult challenge in this stage is keeping Hazuku at bay, all the while dealing with the peons and killing the zombies as soon as possible before they mess up your line of units. For this reason, [[Zombie Killer]] units are heavily recommended. Do not bring [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] as he is too slow to get past Hazuku's attacks. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is amazing here to do good damage to the Wild Doges and Hazuku, although [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] can do better against Hazuku than Courier. Money can be pretty tight, since the only source of cash in this stage are the very limited Sir Seals, but you shouldn't bring a Rich Cat unless things get dire, since it's somewhat easy to burst down and kill Pterowl Hazuku safely after the initial wave of enemies.

